    {
      "id": "5vrWWym7_V6aviszOFoZv",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4155.137351494433,
      "y": 71.30895721783645,
      "width": 1753.3870849609375,
      "height": 1050,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4w",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1287886446,
      "version": 1272,
      "versionNonce": 15427069,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784126536333,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Deep dive\n\nshorten logic\nURL - short(5-7char)\n      - fast\n       - unique\n 1B urls\n\n1) take the prefix of long URL\n     - lot of duplicates as domain maybe same\n2) generate random number\n     - random number - base 62 encode ( 0-9, A-Z, a-z)\n            - with 6 char length it produce - 62^6= 56B unique values\n     - collision prodem with random generator , general 880k collision happens for 1B attemps\n     - to avoids this after encode we need to check the DB, if the key present we retry url shorten logic \n-> increase latency  for repeated attemps\n    \n3)hash the long URl\n    - hash(url) - base62 encode\n     -  similar collision happens here also\n4) counter\n     - increment the counter -> base62\n    - predictablity  -  security risk , with base62 decode of counter data can be leaked\n        - warns user before shortner , ensure rate limit to avoid the data scraping\n    - to reduce latency - precalulate the unique ID generation in batch eg 1000 ids\n             - one downside is if the instance goes down , the unused Id are lost  that's worth the tradeoff\n    - counter may become SPOF - if we add multiple counter instance leads to concurrency issues, we can set range for each one\n\n     \n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Deep dive\n\nshorten logic\nURL - short(5-7char)\n      - fast\n       - unique\n 1B urls\n\n1) take the prefix of long URL\n     - lot of duplicates as domain maybe same\n2) generate random number\n     - random number - base 62 encode ( 0-9, A-Z, a-z)\n            - with 6 char length it produce - 62^6= 56B unique values\n     - collision prodem with random generator , general 880k collision happens for 1B attemps\n     - to avoids this after encode we need to check the DB, if the key present we retry url shorten logic \n-> increase latency  for repeated attemps\n    \n3)hash the long URl\n    - hash(url) - base62 encode\n     -  similar collision happens here also\n4) counter\n     - increment the counter -> base62\n    - predictablity  -  security risk , with base62 decode of counter data can be leaked\n        - warns user before shortner , ensure rate limit to avoid the data scraping\n    - to reduce latency - precalulate the unique ID generation in batch eg 1000 ids\n             - one downside is if the instance goes down , the unused Id are lost  that's worth the tradeoff\n    - counter may become SPOF - if we add multiple counter instance leads to concurrency issues, we can set range for each one\n\n     \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
